  "prefLabel": "He-P 1909.02 Determining Eligibility and Approval for a Waiver",
  "priorExpiration": "2018-11-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 1909.02 Determining Eligibility and Approval for a Waiver.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 155:75, III, the commissioner shall determine eligibility for a waiver.\n\n(b) A person in charge shall be determined to be eligible for a waiver if the following criteria are met:\n\n(1) The waiver request requirements described in He-P 1909.01 are met;\n\n(2) The waiver request is not in response to a finding of a violation of the Act;\n\n(3) The waiver request is not contrary to fire, safety, or sanitation requirements or other state or federal statutes; and\n\n(4) The waiver, if granted, would not create a condition whereby smoke causes harm or unreasonably intrudes into any areas designated as no-smoking or any areas occupied by persons who do not smoke.\n\nSource. #9054, eff 12-29-07, EXPIRED: 12-29-15\n\nNew. #12534, INTERIM, eff 5-24-18, EXPIRES: 11-20-18; ss by #12677, eff 11-20-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p1900.html"
